cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, and also cite the original paper by
  Fu, Wang and Chen listed under references.
type: software
title: >-
  Coordinated Multi-Agent Patrolling with State-Dependent Cost Rates:
  A Python Reimplementation
authors:
  - family-names: Jhawar
    given-names: Achal
    affiliation: RMIT University
  - family-names: Nayak
    given-names: Pratham
    affiliation: RMIT University
  - family-names: Kamalakannan
    given-names: Deepak
    affiliation: RMIT University
repository-code: "https://github.com/achaljhawar/capstone"
abstract: >-
  A Python reimplementation of the C++ code released with Fu, Wang and Chen,
  "Coordinated Multiagent Patrolling With State-Dependent Cost Rates: Asymptotically
  Optimal Policies for Large-Scale Systems" (IEEE Transactions on Automatic Control,
  2025). It builds the paper's synthetic patrol instances, solves the relaxed problem
  as a linear program with HiGHS, and simulates the MAI index policy and a greedy
  baseline. On the same LP solution it reproduces the original program's result rows
  and trajectory logs at full double precision. The repository also reruns the
  paper's Section VI experiments and documents where the shared code and the paper
  differ.
keywords:
  - multi-agent patrolling
  - restless multi-armed bandits
  - index policy
  - Lagrangian relaxation
  - linear programming
  - asymptotic optimality
  - reproducibility
  - reimplementation
